                %rect#svg_39424_16{:fill => "#ffdddd", :height => "20", :stroke => "#000000", "stroke-width" => "2", :width => "20", :x => "0", :y => "90"}
                %rect#svg_39424_17{:fill => "#ffdddd", :height => "20", :stroke => "#000000", "stroke-width" => "2", :width => "20", :x => "0", :y => "110"}
          %ul
            %li
              A skew diagram is called
              %strong connected
              if all boxes share an edge.
            %li
              A skew diagram is called a
              %strong horizontal strip
              if every column contains at most one box.
            %li
              A skew diagram is called a
              %strong vertical strip
              if every row contains at most one box.
            %li conjugation, weight, length extend to skew diagrams accordingly.
